# Line endings for files that are executed rather than read.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux. A shell script
# checked out with CRLF fails on the box with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env
# bash^M`, which is an obscure way to find out that a deploy timer never ran.
# systemd parses unit files line by line and is no happier with a stray CR.
#
# Committed blobs are currently LF, so this pins what is already true rather
# than fixing a break - the point is that it stays true after somebody edits one
# of these in an editor that defaults to CRLF.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf

# Parquet is the archive. Never touch it: these are binary, and a newline
# "fix" inside one would corrupt a season silently.
*.parquet binary
*.npy     binary
*.pt      binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.mp4     binary
